D. §6 Related Work（+0.15 页）

原文 “Foundation Model (FM) Based Approaches” 那段里有一句 “an effective multi-modal foundation model tailored specifically for RAN remains largely unexplored”。现在有了 TimeRAN 这些工作，这句已经不成立，要改。整段替换成：

Pretrained Model Based Approaches. Pretrained models that learn transferable representations from large-scale data and adapt to downstream tasks have been explored across many domains [1, 2, 13, 19, 32, 36] and, more recently, in networking. NetLLM [38] adapts LLMs to networking applications, but LLM-only adaptation performs poorly on regression-based time-series forecasting, a core RAN task. NetGPT [X] and NetMamba [X] pretrain models on network traffic for traffic understanding and classification. Concurrent work on RAN focuses on time-series telemetry: TimeRAN [X] pretrains a lightweight time-series foundation model on an open corpus of RAN telemetry for anomaly detection, classification, forecasting, and imputation, with a proof-of-concept deployment in a 5G testbed. In contrast, RAN-MP jointly models configuration parameters, long-term performance indicators, and KPI time series from a production network, and targets configuration and energy decisions evaluated in field deployment. Recent time-series studies also combine LLM-derived representations with dedicated temporal models rather than relying on LLMs alone [4, 22, 29], supporting RAN-MP’s design: a RAN-specific backbone learns structured numerical and temporal representations, while the LLM module provides complementary semantic and contextual features.

