F. §5.3.1 EngCon（原文两段约 250 词 → 一段约 130 词）

EngCon: Table 4 reports the same metrics with StatF-MLP as the baseline. RAN-MP-Pro achieves the best performance across all metrics, reducing MAPE by 79.9% and RMSE by 26.4%. RAN-MP-Core reduces MAPE to 0.591 and achieves lower errors at all reported percentiles, but its RMSE is slightly above the baseline (1.037) because of a small number of large tail errors, as shown by the error CDF in Figure 5(d). TPB-TM and TPB-TTMs reduce MAPE but perform worse than the baseline on RMSE and the percentile metrics, while NetLLM underperforms on all measures. Overall, RAN-MP’s domain-specific representations enable accurate weekly eNodeB-level energy prediction.

G. §3.1 System Overview（开头加四个要点，约 270 词 → 约 150 词）

保留了每个模块做什么，也注明了对应的小节；删掉的是 “generic, transferable”、"succinct yet potent" 这类描述，以及四个要点各自的展开。

To address the RAN profiling problem and the challenges above, we present RAN-MP (Figure 2). At its core is RAN-MP-Base, a multimodal backbone pretrained on large-scale, unlabeled RAN property and measurement data to learn transferable representations, which can then be adapted to diverse downstream tasks with limited labeled data. RAN-MP-Base encodes RAN property data with a tabular encoder and measurement data with a time-series encoder (Section 3.2.1), fuses the resulting embeddings through cross-attention into a unified representation of each sector’s property states and performance patterns (Section 3.2.2), and is pretrained with a self-supervised objective (Section 3.3). In parallel, a pretrained LLM extracts semantic and contextual features that complement this RAN-specific representation (Section 3.4 and Table 1). During fine-tuning (Section 3.5), RAN-MP-Pro combines both representations, whereas RAN-MP-Core uses only the RAN-MP-Base representation for lightweight adaptation.

