保留：MAPE 降 14%、中位数误差降 10% 这两个最关键的数，NetLLM 在回归任务上不行，Pro 优于 Core 说明 LLM 特征有互补作用，以及 CDF 和运营意义。各个分位数的具体值表里都有，正文就不再列了。

EngSav: Table 3 reports the MAPE, RMSE, and the 25th, 50th, and 75th percentile errors, normalized by the production baseline StatF-MLP. RAN-MP-Pro achieves the smallest error across all metrics, reducing MAPE by 14% and the median error by 10% relative to StatF-MLP, a production solution used for years, and RAN-MP-Core also outperforms the baseline on all metrics. Unlike RANPerf, this fine-grained regression task exposes the limitations of existing pretrained models, including NetLLM, underscoring the importance of RAN-specific numerical and temporal representations, while the gain of RAN-MP-Pro over RAN-MP-Core indicates that LLM-derived features remain complementary. Figure 5(c) shows the CDF of the normalized absolute error: RAN-MP-Pro and RAN-MP-Core achieve the smallest error at every percentile, enabling operators to optimize cell-sleeping decisions while maintaining service quality.

